This project reuses ideas and file formats from the following open-source projects. No third-party source
code is vendored in this repository.

1. ECC (Everything Claude Code) - https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC
   Copyright (c) 2026 Affaan Mustafa. MIT License.
   Used for: the instinct file format and skill-run record format read by `skillevo import-ecc`
   (src/skillevo/importers.py follows the instinct file layout used by ECC's instinct-cli.py), and the design
   idea of per-skill version snapshots with rollback (reimplemented in Python in src/skillevo/versioning.py).
   ECC is NOT a dependency. It is only fetched by scripts/fetch_ecc_corpus.py as an optional test corpus,
   into a git-ignored directory, pinned to a specific commit.

2. anthropics/skills (skill-creator) - https://github.com/anthropics/skills
   Apache License 2.0.
   Used for: the shape of evals.json (examples/evals.json is a simplified variant) and the general skill
   naming/description rules. The validation rules in src/skillevo/skills.py are an independent, deliberately
   more lenient reimplementation; no code was copied.

3. claude-mem - https://github.com/thedotmack/claude-mem (Apache License 2.0)
   Design reference only (SQLite + FTS5 storage with a budgeted injection at session start). No code used.

